==========================================================================================
  KNOWN BOTTLENECKS — DETECTED CPU + GPU PLATFORM
==========================================================================================

  ⚠  Host PCIe (data ingestion)
     Bottleneck : PCIe 5.0 ×16 = 63 GB/s per GPU << HBM3 = 3350 GB/s
     Ratio      : 32x HBM/PCIe
     Mitigation : Use in-GPU preprocessing, NVLink-based data redistribution, or PCIe switches.

  ⚠  CPU DRAM bandwidth
     Bottleneck : CPU DRAM peak = 614 GB/s << HBM3 total = 4000 GB/s
     Ratio      : 7x HBM/DRAM
     Mitigation : Pre-process data on GPU, use NUMA-local allocation, or async prefetch.

  ⚠  CPU FP32 vs GPU FP32
     Bottleneck : CPU FP32 turbo = 56 TFLOPS << GPU total FP32 = 134 TFLOPS
     Ratio      : 2x GPU/CPU
     Mitigation : Offload all FP32 workloads to GPU; CPU handles orchestration only.

  ⚠  NVLink fabric (GPU-to-GPU)
     Bottleneck : NVLink total BW = 1800 GB/s — not a bottleneck vs HBM but limits all-reduce in training
     Ratio      : 0.90x NVLink/HBM
     Mitigation : Overlap all-reduce with compute; use ring-all-reduce or NCCL overlap.

  ⚠  Memory-bound kernels (low AI)
     Bottleneck : Any kernel with AI < 378 FLOP/byte is HBM-bandwidth-limited on H100
     Ratio      : Roofline knee = 378 FLOP/byte
     Mitigation : Fuse kernels to increase arithmetic intensity; use Flash Attention.

